# Build context exclusions for docs-site/Dockerfile.
#
# ⚠️ node_modules IS A CORRECTNESS EXCLUSION HERE, NOT JUST A SIZE ONE.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY package*.json ./` -> `RUN npm ci` -> `COPY . .` (the standard
# cache-the-dependency-layer shape frontend/Dockerfile.prod also uses). Without this file,
# that final `COPY . .` overwrites the /app/node_modules the `npm ci` layer just built with
# the HOST's tree — which was installed for the host's platform and Node version, not the
# build stage's node:26-alpine. It also invalidates the cached dependency layer on every
# source change, so `npm ci` re-runs regardless.
#
# Size, measured on this checkout: docs-site is 1.1 GB across 40,164 files, of which
# node_modules is 918 MB / 39,171 files and build/ is 64 MB. Every one of those bytes was
# being uploaded to the daemon on every `docker build`, only to be discarded.
#
# The three excluded directories are exactly the ones the image REBUILDS: `npm ci` recreates
# node_modules, `npm run build` recreates build/ and .docusaurus/.
#
# scripts/release-tests/lib/compose-patch.sh's cp_stage_docs_context excludes the same three
# for the rehearsal's `cp` of this tree — a .dockerignore does not govern `cp`, so both are
# needed and they are kept in step deliberately.

# Dependencies (see the note above — correctness, not just size)
node_modules/

# Docusaurus build outputs
build/
.docusaurus/

# Environment
.env
.env.*

# VCS / editor / OS
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Docker itself
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore

# Logs and caches
*.log
.cache/
.npm/
